Subject: [PATCH 154/175] feat: asset pickers on both LUT slots, and a grade
 preset you can export and reuse (S10 item 4b)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The component half of item 4b: 「我需要這些東西都有導出導入重用的功能」 and
「現成的那些填入 cube 的欄位，做成可以選擇檔案的形式」.

PICKERS. Output -> ODT File and Look -> LMT File move from Schematyc::CineCubeFileName
(SResourceNameSerializer -> a plain file dialog) to Schematyc::CineLutFileName
(SResourceNameSelector on the CineLut asset type -> the Asset Browser). The stored value
is unchanged: ResourceSelector's yasli Serialize decorates only in an edit archive and
otherwise writes the plain string, byte for byte what the file-path family wrote. So no
level data migrates. Two stock limitations of the old row go away with it - the dialog
could only offer files under the project, and it dropped the decorator's start folder.

PRESET. A fourth reflected group, Preset, holding a .cinegrade asset picker and two
buttons (Export Preset, Re-apply Preset). The file is XML written over the SAME reflected
structs the inspector uses (Schematyc::Utils::SerializeClass), so a control added to the
component next month lands in every preset for free and the XML's element names are the
member names. It carries the wheels and their masters, contrast and pivot, saturation,
the ASC CDL base, both curves, the LMT reference with its input space, and the bypass.
Export writes Assets/cinecam/grades/<entity>.cinegrade AND its .cryasset, by hand, so the
file is a registered asset the moment it exists - no editor, no RC, no waiting.

COPY ON APPLY, IN THE ONE SAFE WINDOW. Picking a preset overwrites Grade, Curves and Look
and the component then owns the values; the path stays only as source information. The
apply runs inside the component's own INPUT serialization, from a member declared LAST.
That is deliberate and it is the whole design: EntityObject.cpp:928 takes the snapshot the
level is saved from AFTER the input pass at :912 and BEFORE the property-changed event at
:931, which is why item 3a refuses to write derived values back from the handler.
Schematyc serialises members in AddMember order, so a member after Grade/Curves/Look can
legally overwrite all three and still be inside that snapshot. Picking then triggers
apply() followed by revert(), so the inspector redraws with the new numbers and the undo
transaction covers the whole component. The apply is gated on archive.isEdit(), so a level
load never re-applies - that is what makes it a copy and not a live link.
The two buttons do not run inside an input pass, so they re-run the editor's snapshot by
hand (the pair of calls at EntityObject.cpp:925/928, reachable from the engine side
through GetSchematycObject()->GetObjectProperties()->GetComponentProperties()).

FOLDER MOVE. kDefaultODTFile and the two hard-coded wrap ODT paths follow the files into
Assets/cinecam/luts (and .../system for the inverse). OpenLutFile gains ONE fallback,
after both real lookups have failed: a stale Assets/ODT/... path is retried under the new
folders and logs one line. Levels saved before today are unaffected.

CAPTURE OUTPUTS. New command cinecam_ImportGradeAssets [folder] copies a take's .cdl and
.cube (and any .curves.txt) out of the EXR capture folder under %USER% and into
Assets/cinecam/cdl and Assets/cinecam/luts with sidecars. A command and not automatic: a
take belongs beside its frames and an EXR sequence is not an asset.

Renderer untouched. New files: Module/CineGradeAsset.{h,cpp}.
Docs: README (Output/Look/Preset tables, the picker paragraph),
docs/SceneReferredLook.md (new section 5, the folder listing), docs/SceneReferredExport.md
(new section 4.3), docs/ConsoleReference.md (cinecam_ImportGradeAssets).

Research: scene-notes/research/s10-4b-asset-system.md
Decisions: scene-notes/decisions/s10-grade-component.md section 4b.4 - 4b.7

